'''Kaimbé''' is an extinct [[unclassified language]] of eastern Brazil. The ethnic population numbered an estimated 1,100 to 1,400 in 1986. The language is scarcely attested; in 1961 one elder was able to remember a few single words mixed with [[Kiriri language|Kiriri]].

The district of Caimbé in [[Euclides da Cunha, Bahia]] is named after the tribe.

